{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovUnusedGenerator"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.not_kappa_eq_zero_iff_dvd_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.not_kappa_eq_zero_iff_dvd_six","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L106-L117","doc":"**C-5a fails for the strand tower.** For every Markov-trace tower over a\ndomain, whatever the Markov parameter, it is false that `κ_n = 0 ↔ n ∣ 6`\nfor all `n ≥ 1`: levels `1` and `4` would need opposite answers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.kappa_zero_set_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.kappa_zero_set_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L83-L104","doc":"Over a domain, on the levels `n ≥ 1` the zero set of `κ` is all of them or\nnone of them. (Level `0` can differ only when `z = 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.kappa_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.kappa_eq","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L77-L81","doc":"`κ_n = (z − 1) · z^n · tr 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.tr_rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.tr_rCheck","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L69-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.kappa","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The level-`n` obstruction `κ_n = tr(Ř_(n+1) − ℓ_n Ř_(n))`, with `ℓ_n` the\nstrand inclusion (the identity on the ambient algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.rCheck_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.rCheck_mem","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L59-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.rCheck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrandTowerObstruction.rCheck","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StrandTowerObstruction.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The strand-tower R-matrix: `Ř_0 = 1`, `Ř_(n+1) = Ř_(n) · σ_n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}